<node id="paper_broad_1f5f4154830ff7beb2d8">
  <data key="d17">Paper</data>
  <data key="d18">Reaction intermediates during operando electrocatalysis identified from full solvent quantum mechanics molecular dynamics</data>
  <data key="d19"></data>
</node>
<node id="reaction_co2_reduction">
  <data key="d17">Reaction</data>
  <data key="d18">Carbon dioxide reduction reaction</data>
  <data key="d19">Electrocatalytic carbon dioxide reduction reaction studied under operando conditions.</data>
</node>
<node id="environment_electrode_electrolyte">
  <data key="d17">InterfacialEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d18">Electrode–electrolyte interface with explicit solvent and applied voltage</data>
  <data key="d19">The simulated operando electrode–electrolyte interface includes explicit solvent and an applied voltage.</data>
</node>
<node id="intermediates_co2rr_reactive">
  <data key="d17">Intermediate</data>
  <data key="d18">Reactive CO2RR intermediates</data>
  <data key="d19">Reactive intermediates identified and distinguished for the carbon dioxide reduction reaction.</data>
</node>
<node id="calc_full_solvent_qm_md">
  <data key="d17">Calculation</data>
  <data key="d18">Full-solvent quantum mechanics molecular dynamics of the electrode–electrolyte interface</data>
  <data key="d20">quantum_mechanics_molecular_dynamics</data>
  <data key="d21">[]</data>
  <data key="d22">QM-based simulation with explicit solvent and applied voltage; reactive trajectories are generated for subsequent vibrational-density-of-states analysis.</data>
</node>
<node id="calc_two_phase_thermodynamics_vdos">
  <data key="d17">Calculation</data>
  <data key="d18">Two-phase thermodynamics vibrational-density-of-states analysis</data>
  <data key="d20">vibrational_density_of_states_calculation</data>
  <data key="d21">[]</data>
  <data key="d22">Two-phase thermodynamics model applied to reactive trajectories to generate vibrational densities of states for comparison with experimental spectroscopy.</data>
</node>
<node id="obs_distinguished_co2rr_intermediates">
  <data key="d17">ObservationClaim</data>
  <data key="d18">Reactive intermediates in the carbon dioxide reduction reaction were distinguished by resolving simulated vibrational signals for comparison with reported experimental spectroscopy.</data>
  <data key="d23">intermediate_identification</data>
  <data key="d24">Reactive intermediates in the carbon dioxide reduction reaction were distinguished by resolving simulated vibrational signals for comparison with reported experimental spectroscopy.</data>
  <data key="d25">computational</data>
  <data key="d19">The abstract reports successful distinction of reactive CO2RR intermediates using the solvent- and voltage-inclusive simulation workflow.</data>
</node>
<node id="mech_atomic_scale_co2rr_understanding">
  <data key="d17">MechanismClaim</data>
  <data key="d18">Explicit consideration of solvent and applied voltage at the electrode–electrolyte interface enables reactive-trajectory and vibrational-signal analysis that provides atomic-scale understanding of the carbon dioxide reduction reaction.</data>
  <data key="d23">atomic_scale_mechanistic_understanding</data>
  <data key="d24">Explicit consideration of solvent and applied voltage at the electrode–electrolyte interface enables reactive-trajectory and vibrational-signal analysis that provides atomic-scale understanding of the carbon dioxide reduction reaction.</data>
  <data key="d25">computational</data>
  <data key="d19">This is the authors' stated interpretation of the operando QM simulation approach and its identification of reactive intermediates.</data>
</node>
